    {
      "text": "Half of the Mo content should be replaced by V to form NbZrTiHfMo0.5V0.5.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Partial replacement of Mo by V will reduce the alloy's overall electronegativity difference.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "NbZrTiHfMo0.5V0.5 will remain a homogeneous, disordered, single-phase BCC solid solution under the proposed processing conditions.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Moderating electronegativity differences through V substitution will reduce lattice distortion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "V has a lower electronegativity than Mo.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Introducing V will decrease local bond heterogeneity.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Decreased local bond heterogeneity will lower intrinsic barriers to dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower barriers to dislocation motion will enhance room-temperature plastic deformation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The V-substituted alloy will retain substantial solid-solution strengthening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "NbZrTiHfMo0.5V0.5 will have a room-temperature compressive yield strength of approximately 1600–1700 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "NbZrTiHfMo0.5V0.5 will exhibit a 20–30% increase in compressive plastic strain relative to equiatomic NbZrTiHfMo.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The beneficial strength–plasticity effect is conditional on retention of a single-phase disordered BCC structure.",
